@startuml DCP_Credential_Offer_preceding_Issuance_with_Presentation
autonumber

participant "Secure Token Service\n(Holder)" as STS
participant "Client\n(Holder)" as Client
participant "Credential Service\n(Holder)" as CS
participant "Issuer Service\n(Issuer)" as Issuer
participant "Secure Token Service \n (Issuer)" as STS_Issuer

== (issuer-initiated) Credential Offer ==

note right of Issuer
  An out-of-band trigger (e.g. key
  rotation / revocation → reissue, or a
  business event) prompts the Issuer to
  offer a credential to the Holder.
  The Issuer resolves the Holder's DID
  to discover its Credential Service
  endpoint.
end note

Issuer -> Issuer: resolve Holder DID → find CS endpoint

Issuer -> STS_Issuer: request token
activate STS_Issuer
STS_Issuer --> Issuer: Self-Issued ID Token (SI Token)
deactivate STS_Issuer

Issuer -> CS : POST /offers\nCredentialOfferMessage\nw/ issuer DID + credentials[]\n(each a CredentialObject,\n incl. issuancePolicy)
activate CS
note right of CS
  The CredentialOfferMessage carries one or
  more CredentialObjects. A CredentialObject
  MAY embed an **issuancePolicy** (a
  Presentation Definition) that signals the
  Verifiable Presentation the Holder will be
  REQUIRED to provide during issuance.
end note
CS -> CS: store / surface offer to Holder
CS --> Issuer: HTTP 200 OK
deactivate CS

== Holder acts on the Offer ==

note left of Client
  The Holder decides to act on the offer notification.
  It reads the offered CredentialObject(s)
  and their ids from the stored offer
  (sparse entries resolve against the
  Issuer Metadata credentialsSupported list).
  This interaction is not standardized and optional.
end note

Client -> CS : read stored offer
activate CS
CS --> Client : CredentialObject(s) w/ id + issuancePolicy
deactivate CS

note over Client, Issuer
  From here the Holder runs the canonical Issuance Flow,
  referencing the offered CredentialObject id(s).
  The Verifiable Presentation defined by the
  issuancePolicy is provided as proof for issuance.
end note

Client -> STS: request
activate STS
STS -> Client: response incl. access token
deactivate STS

Client -> Issuer: request credential(s) w/ self-issued ID token incl. access token\n(CredentialRequestMessage, credentials[].id from the offer)
activate Issuer
Issuer -> Issuer: resolve DID
Client <- Issuer: ack

CS <- Issuer: (async) write credential(s)\nw/ self-issued ID token access token
activate CS
CS -> CS: Validate token and\nstore credentials
deactivate CS
deactivate Issuer

@enduml
